  "body": "Worklets have moved from CSS Houdini to HTML. I'd like to use this issue to consolidate:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/47\r\n- https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/376\r\n- https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/979\r\n\r\nThe idea on the table is to provide a way to load code into worklets without using JavaScript.\r\n\r\nA summary of those discussions from what I can see:\r\n\r\n- People would like some sort of \"inline\" form in your HTML page. However, this is pretty problematic. See e.g. https://github.com/w3c/css-houdini-drafts/issues/376#issuecomment-292699344 and surrounding comments. In particular, using the `<script>` element for something with extremely different semantics from other `<script>` types is tricky. (See also #4786, which is the corresponding issue for workers. If we were to do anything here, we should probably do them together.)\r\n\r\n- The latest thinking seems to be `<link rel=\"paintworklet\" href=\"foo.mjs\">`.",
